/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Workflows_Test Test
 * @ingroup Foundation_Workflows_Development
 * @brief Build a testing preset and execute its CTest suite.
 *
 * The test workflow performs three operations in order:
 *
 * 1. configures the selected preset with `FOUNDATION_TESTING=ON`;
 * 2. builds the selected configuration;
 * 3. runs CTest from `build/<preset>` with failure output enabled.
 *
 * `FOUNDATION_TESTING=ON` is present in the active cache immediately after this
 * workflow. A later script configuration reapplies preset-defined defaults, but
 * a fresh export is still recommended for release packaging because unrelated
 * feature overrides may remain cached.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowTestBash Bash
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * ./scripts/test.sh <preset> [--config <name>] \
 *     [--parallel <jobs>] [--filter <regex>] [--fresh] [--allow-no-tests]
 *
 * ./scripts/test.sh macos_arm64 --config Debug --parallel 8
 * ./scripts/test.sh macos_arm64 --filter TimePoint
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowTestArguments Arguments and Defaults
 *
 * Test defaults to `Debug`. The filter is forwarded as CTest's regular
 * expression, parallel controls both compilation and CTest workers, and fresh
 * recreates the cache before enabling testing. Test failures propagate as a
 * nonzero script exit status.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowTestPowerShell PowerShell
 *
 * @code{powershell}
 * ./scripts/test.ps1 <preset> [-Configuration <name>] `
 *     [-Parallel <jobs>] [-Filter <regex>] [-Fresh] [-AllowNoTests]
 * @endcode
 *
 * Test output is always displayed on failure. An empty CTest suite is an error
 * by default so a release cannot silently pass without validation.
 * `--allow-no-tests` or `-AllowNoTests` exists only for diagnosing a deliberate
 * configuration that registers no tests and must not be used by a release gate.
 * The test workflow enables only `FOUNDATION_TESTING` while configuring the
 * selected target preset; a separate testing preset is not needed. Examples are
 * API demonstrations and are never enabled, executed, or reported as tests by
 * this workflow.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowTestSuite Registered Native Suite
 *
 * The default feature set builds seven module-scoped GoogleTest executables:
 *
 * - `FoundationMathTests`;
 * - `FoundationTypeTraitsTests`;
 * - `FoundationUtilsTests`;
 * - `FoundationContainersTests`;
 * - `FoundationFunctionalTests`;
 * - `FoundationTimeTests`;
 * - `FoundationSchedulingTests`.
 *
 * `gtest_discover_tests()` exposes every `TEST()` case separately to CTest. Each
 * executable uses Foundation's public headers, lives below the matching
 * `tests/Foundation/<module>` directory, and is registered only when all modules
 * it requires are enabled. Use `--filter <regex>` or `-Filter <regex>` to select
 * discovered cases by name without changing the build graph.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowTestDependency GoogleTest Dependency
 *
 * `cmake/BuildTests.cmake` obtains GoogleTest 1.18.0 through CMake
 * `FetchContent`, pinned to the release commit rather than a moving branch.
 * A clean first configuration therefore needs access to GitHub unless the
 * dependency has already been populated or a standard FetchContent source
 * override is supplied. GoogleTest and GoogleMock installation are disabled;
 * none of their headers or libraries enter a Foundation package. With
 * `FOUNDATION_TESTING=OFF`, GoogleTest is neither downloaded nor added to the
 * build graph.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowTestNativeVsCross Native and Cross Tests
 *
 * Native presets may build and execute CTest programs on the host. Cross presets
 * create binaries for a different processor and cannot be treated as host
 * executable tests. AVR, STM32, PSoC, and generic Arm targets require one of:
 *
 * - tests compiled into the consuming firmware and executed on hardware;
 * - a target-aware emulator with an explicit CMake/CTest launcher;
 * - host-side tests built from the same portable source using a native preset.
 *
 * Validate embedded outputs with @ref Foundation_Workflows_Validation and do
 * not report `AllowNoTests` as a successful test suite.
 */
